From 5930f791b9055cdbf62664fbd99ee4c8b78de605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geckomacabre <91030858+Geckomacabre@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:03:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] VICTORY_MAX_STEP_MS=<ms> (off): raise the title's longest
 simulation step so the world keeps real speed at low frame rates

The title's timer step (+0x2226040) is max(min(dt, 1/15 s), 1/30 s); +0x8dec0 clamps
the world update's step to 1/15 s again, and the paused branch of +0x22264d0 too. So a
frame longer than 66.7 ms moves the world only 66.7 ms: at 8 fps it runs at about half
speed, at 4 fps at a quarter. The 1/15 s constant has 64 readers, so it stays; the
three vmovss loads are pointed at a float of ours in the int3 padding after
+0x2226040's ret (+0x2226128). Every site's whole instruction is compared first, all or
nothing, and only on the known build (written in memory after load).
VICTORY_MAX_STEP_MS takes 66.7 to 333 ms (100 is a good value); longer steps mean more
of the title's 1/15 s physics substeps per frame. VICTORY_STEP_LOG=1 logs game time
against wall time every 5 s, with or without the patch.

Needs the known build entry (pull request for the Series S upscaler choice).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
